## Target
Add a new module `crates/kanban-domain/src/archival.rs` (declared `pub mod archival;` in `lib.rs`, re-export the trait + envelope) with a **thin** envelope + key trait — **and NO `ArchiveCollection`** (validated-dead, dropped):

```rust
// crates/kanban-domain/src/archival.rs
use chrono::{DateTime, Utc};
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use uuid::Uuid;

/// Shared archival metadata envelope. Common to every archived entity;
/// the entity-specific restore context is NOT stored here (stays on the
/// concrete archived type, e.g. ArchivedCard::original_column_id).
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct ArchiveMetadata {
    pub archived_at: DateTime<Utc>,
}

impl ArchiveMetadata {
    pub fn now() -> Self {
        Self { archived_at: Utc::now() }
    }
    pub fn at(archived_at: DateTime<Utc>) -> Self {
        Self { archived_at }
    }
}

/// A discrete archived record: knows the live entity's stable id (its archive
/// key) and its shared metadata. Payload beyond this stays specialized on the
/// concrete type — the trait covers the envelope + key, not the payload (D9).
pub trait ArchivedEntity {
    /// Stable id of the live entity this record archives (card id / board id).
    fn entity_id(&self) -> Uuid;
    fn metadata(&self) -> ArchiveMetadata;
    fn archived_at(&self) -> DateTime<Utc> {
        self.metadata().archived_at
    }
}
```

> **NO `ArchiveCollection` trait.** Both spikes proved no backend would implement a store-generic archive collection — stores keep hand-rolled per-entity `DataStore` methods (`insert_archived_card`, `list_archived_cards_by_board`, etc.). Adding it would be the "wrong abstraction" the Phase 7 gate warns against. `ArchivedEntity::entity_id()` earns its keep at exactly one call site (the in-memory archive-key read in B2); `ArchiveMetadata` is the seam for a future `archived_by`/reason. That is the whole abstraction.

