## Entity-specific quirks
- DUAL minting: `sprint_number` (from `Board.sprint_counters` via `get_next_sprint_number`/`ensure_sprint_counter_initialized`) AND `name_index` (from `Board.sprint_names`/`sprint_name_used_count` via `add_sprint_name_at_used_index`/`consume_sprint_name`). Both minted at the service tier and injected — the domain `create` never touches the Board. This is the Sprint analogue of Card's single `card_number` seed.
- `auto_consume_name` (`sprint_commands.rs:276,296`) is a TUI-only behaviour (consume next pooled name when none supplied). Preserve it: the create input must carry an `auto_consume_name`/name-source flag so the service knows whether to `consume_sprint_name()` vs leave `name_index=None`. CLI/MCP pass false today (`sprint_commands.rs:275-276` doc).
- Board mutation is a service-tier side effect of sprint creation; it persists `board_sprint_counters`/`board_sprint_names` via the Board write path (slice B of the Board epic) — keep the `upsert_board` before `upsert_sprint`.
- The `CreateSprint` command's `capture_inverse` (delete the sprint, leaving counters bumped — `sprint_commands.rs:316-325`) must keep working after the refactor; redo reproduces the same id.

## Implementation sketch (before -> after)

The dual minting (`sprint_number` from the Board's counters, `name_index` from the Board's name pool) stays at the service tier, the only layer that owns both the Board and the store and where `id`/`now` are injected. The domain factory stays I/O-free and Board-free: it receives the two already-minted server values as plain arguments.

### BEFORE — mint in the command, `Sprint::new` then overwrite id

`KanbanContext::create_sprint_impl` mints the id and dispatches a command (`crates/kanban-service/src/context/sprints.rs:44-70`):

```rust
pub(super) fn create_sprint_impl(
    &mut self,
    board_id: Uuid,
    prefix: Option<String>,
    name: Option<String>,
) -> KanbanResult<Sprint> {
    use kanban_domain::commands::CreateSprint;

    let default_sprint_prefix = self.app_config.effective_default_sprint_prefix().to_string();

    let id = Uuid::new_v4();
    let cmd = Command::Sprint(SprintCommand::Create(CreateSprint {
        id,
        board_id,
        name,
        default_sprint_prefix,
        explicit_prefix: prefix,
        auto_consume_name: false,
    }));
    self.execute(vec![cmd])?;
    self.get_sprint_impl(id)?.ok_or_else(|| {
        KanbanError::Internal("Sprint creation succeeded but sprint not found".into())
    })
}
```

`CreateSprint::execute` does the Board minting AND the create-then-mutate kludge (`crates/kanban-domain/src/commands/sprint_commands.rs:280-310`):

```rust
pub fn execute(&self, context: &CommandContext) -> KanbanResult<()> {
    let sprints_snapshot = context.store.list_sprints_by_board(self.board_id)?;

    let mut board = context.get_board(self.board_id)?;
    let effective_prefix = self
        .explicit_prefix
        .clone()
        .or_else(|| board.sprint_prefix.clone())
        .unwrap_or_else(|| self.default_sprint_prefix.clone());

    board.ensure_sprint_counter_initialized(&effective_prefix, &sprints_snapshot);
    let sprint_number = board.get_next_sprint_number(&effective_prefix);
    let name_index = match &self.name {
        Some(name) if !name.trim().is_empty() => {
            Some(board.add_sprint_name_at_used_index(name.clone()))
        }
        _ if self.auto_consume_name => board.consume_sprint_name(),
        _ => None,
    };

    let mut sprint = crate::Sprint::new(self.board_id, sprint_number, name_index, Some(effective_prefix));
    sprint.id = self.id;                  // <- create-then-mutate kludge
    context.store.upsert_board(board)?;   // counters/pool bumped
    context.store.upsert_sprint(sprint)?; // ordered after the board
    Ok(())
}
```

### AFTER — service mints everything from the Board, domain `Sprint::create` is pure

The minting block (resolve prefix, `ensure_sprint_counter_initialized`, `get_next_sprint_number`, allocate `name_index`) stays in the command's `execute` — which already holds the store and Board — but now feeds `Sprint::create` instead of `Sprint::new` + `sprint.id =`. The FK and client-id checks gate the mint. Board `upsert` stays ordered before the sprint `upsert`, preserving today's persistence ordering and keeping `capture_inverse` valid (delete the sprint, leave counters bumped, redo reproduces the same id):

```rust
pub fn execute(&self, context: &CommandContext) -> KanbanResult<()> {
    // FK existence: board must exist before we mint anything.
    let mut board = context
        .store
        .get_board(self.board_id)?
        .ok_or_else(|| KanbanError::not_found("Board", self.board_id))?;

    // Client-supplied id uniqueness -> conflict (idempotent PUT-create entry point).
    if context.store.get_sprint(self.id)?.is_some() {
        return Err(KanbanError::conflict(format!(
            "Sprint {} already exists",
            self.id
        )));
    }

    let sprints_snapshot = context.store.list_sprints_by_board(self.board_id)?;
    let effective_prefix = self
        .explicit_prefix
        .clone()
        .or_else(|| board.sprint_prefix.clone())
        .unwrap_or_else(|| self.default_sprint_prefix.clone());

    // Dual minting stays at this tier (service owns the Board + store).
    board.ensure_sprint_counter_initialized(&effective_prefix, &sprints_snapshot);
    let sprint_number = board.get_next_sprint_number(&effective_prefix);
    let name_index = match &self.name {
        Some(name) if !name.trim().is_empty() => {
            Some(board.add_sprint_name_at_used_index(name.clone()))
        }
        _ if self.auto_consume_name => board.consume_sprint_name(),
        _ => None,
    };

    // Pure factory: Board-free, I/O-free; receives the minted values.
    let now = Utc::now();
    let spec = NewSprint {
        board_id: self.board_id,
        prefix: Some(effective_prefix),
        card_prefix: None,
    };
    let sprint = crate::Sprint::create(spec, self.id, now, sprint_number, name_index)?;

    context.store.upsert_board(board)?;   // counters/pool persisted first
    context.store.upsert_sprint(sprint)?; // then the sprint (ordering preserved)
    Ok(())
}
```

Net effect: `Sprint::new` + `sprint.id = ..` is deleted (and `Sprint::new` retired once all callers migrate); the only construction paths become `Sprint::create` (new) and `Sprint::reconstitute` (load, slice A/B). The Board mutation remains a service-tier side effect persisted via the Board write path — the domain factory never touches the Board.

