## Target
FormatVersion (`traits.rs`):
```rust
pub enum FormatVersion {
    V1, V2, V3, V4, V5, V6, V7,
    /// V8 promotes archived cards to a first-class discrete collection:
    /// each `archived_cards` entry carries its own `board_id` (backfilled
    /// from `original_column_id`→column→board for historical files) and is
    /// guaranteed not to be duplicated inside the `cards` array.
    V8,
}
impl FormatVersion {
    pub const MAX: Self = Self::V8;
    pub fn as_u32(self) -> u32 { /* ..., Self::V7 => 7, Self::V8 => 8 */ }
    pub fn from_u32(v: u32) -> Option<Self> { /* ..., 8 => Some(Self::V8) */ }
}
```
New transform module `crates/kanban-persistence-json/src/migration/v7_to_v8_archived_cards.rs`:
```rust
/// Pure transform: backfill `board_id` on each archived-card entry from
/// `original_column_id`→`columns[].board_id`, drop any `cards`-array entry
/// that shadows an archived card, and bump the envelope to version 8.
/// Idempotent on `version >= 8`.
pub(crate) fn transform_v7_to_v8_value(envelope: &mut Value) -> PersistenceResult<()>;

/// Async file wrapper: read → transform → atomic write. Output is V8.
pub(crate) async fn migrate_v7_to_v8(path: &Path) -> PersistenceResult<()>;
```
Backup path helper (`backup.rs`) renamed to cover V7 as a migratable source:
```rust
pub(crate) fn pre_latest_backup_path_for(from: FormatVersion, path: &Path) -> Option<PathBuf> {
    match from {
        FormatVersion::V1 => Some(path.with_extension("v1.backup")),
        // ... V2..V6 unchanged ...
        FormatVersion::V7 => Some(path.with_extension("v7.backup")),
        _ => None, // V8 is the target
    }
}
```

