# Slim KanbanBackend by extending the core trait

## Motivation
With `kanban_core::Backend` defined and `InMemoryStore` implementing it, `KanbanBackend` in kanban-service can shed its duplicated lifecycle methods and inherit them from the core trait. The kanban-specific surface stays: `as_data_store()` and `persistence_metadata()`.

## Current state
`crates/kanban-service/src/backend.rs:25-82`:
```rust
#[async_trait]
pub trait KanbanBackend: DataStore + CommandStore + Send + Sync {
    fn as_data_store(&self) -> &dyn DataStore;
    async fn flush(&self) -> KanbanResult<()> { Ok(()) }
    async fn reload(&self) -> KanbanResult<()> { Ok(()) }
    fn needs_flush(&self) -> bool { false }
    fn needs_save_worker(&self) -> bool { false }
    fn instance_id(&self) -> Uuid { Uuid::nil() }
    fn persistence_metadata(&self) -> Option<PersistenceMetadata> { None }
    fn with_transaction(&self, f: &mut dyn FnMut() -> KanbanResult<()>) -> KanbanResult<()> { ... }
}
```

## Target shape
```rust
use kanban_core::Backend;

#[async_trait]
pub trait KanbanBackend:
    Backend<Snapshot = kanban_domain::Snapshot> + DataStore + CommandStore + Send + Sync
{
    fn as_data_store(&self) -> &dyn DataStore;

    /// Metadata about the underlying persistence store. Returns `None` for
    /// in-memory backends. KANBAN-SPECIFIC — references kanban-persistence
    /// types, stays here.
    fn persistence_metadata(&self) -> Option<PersistenceMetadata> { None }
}
```

`KanbanBackend for InMemoryStore` (currently `backend.rs:86-92`) shrinks to:
