# Final composition: KanbanContext as a thin wrapper

## Motivation
The terminal step of the wiring. With Backend, Command, UndoStack, Context, and the BackendExecutor adapter all in place, refactor `KanbanContext` from a monolithic struct that owns the pipeline into a thin wrapper holding `inner: Context<dyn KanbanBackend, Command>`.

Public API of `KanbanContext` is preserved — no source changes needed in kanban-cli, kanban-tui, kanban-mcp, kanban-mcp.

## Current state
`crates/kanban-service/src/context.rs:48-330` has the struct + ~140 lines of lifecycle methods (execute/undo/redo/save/reload/replace_backend/dirty-flag/etc.). Below that (~1100 lines) are `KanbanOperations`, `GraphOperations`, batch helpers — all kanban-specific business logic to be left alone.

## Target shape
```rust
use kanban_core::{AppConfig, Context};

pub struct KanbanContext {
    inner: Context<dyn KanbanBackend, Command>,
    app_config: AppConfig,
    conflict_pending: bool,
}

impl KanbanContext {
    pub fn open_deferred(backend: Arc<dyn KanbanBackend>, config: AppConfig) -> Self {
        Self { inner: Context::new(backend), app_config: config, conflict_pending: false }
    }

    pub async fn open(backend: Arc<dyn KanbanBackend>, config: AppConfig) -> KanbanResult<Self> {
        let ctx = Self::open_deferred(backend, config);
        // Surface lazy-load errors. command_count is on CommandStore (kanban-specific).
        ctx.inner.backend().command_count()?;
        Ok(ctx)
    }

    // ── Pipeline pass-throughs (one line each) ──────────────────────
    pub fn backend(&self) -> Arc<dyn KanbanBackend> { self.inner.backend() }
    pub fn execute(&mut self, cmds: Vec<Command>) -> KanbanResult<()> {
        self.inner.execute(cmds).map_err(KanbanError::from)
    }
    pub fn undo(&mut self) -> KanbanResult<bool> { self.inner.undo().map_err(KanbanError::from) }
    pub fn redo(&mut self) -> KanbanResult<bool> { self.inner.redo().map_err(KanbanError::from) }
    pub fn can_undo(&self) -> bool { self.inner.can_undo() }
    pub fn can_redo(&self) -> bool { self.inner.can_redo() }
    pub fn undo_depth(&self) -> usize { self.inner.undo_depth() }
    pub fn redo_depth(&self) -> usize { self.inner.redo_depth() }
    pub fn clear_history(&mut self) -> KanbanResult<()> { self.inner.clear_history(); Ok(()) }
    pub fn is_dirty(&self) -> bool { self.inner.is_dirty() }
    pub fn mark_dirty(&mut self) { self.inner.mark_dirty() }
    pub fn mark_clean(&mut self) { self.inner.mark_clean() }
    pub async fn save(&self) -> KanbanResult<()> { self.inner.save().await.map_err(KanbanError::from) }
    pub async fn reload(&mut self) -> KanbanResult<()> { self.inner.reload().await.map_err(KanbanError::from) }
    pub fn replace_backend(&mut self, backend: Arc<dyn KanbanBackend>) { self.inner.replace_backend(backend) }

    // ── Kanban-specific accessors (unchanged) ───────────────────────
    pub fn app_config(&self) -> &AppConfig { &self.app_config }
    pub fn data_store(&self) -> &dyn DataStore { self.inner.backend().as_data_store() }
    pub fn persistence_metadata(&self) -> Option<PersistenceMetadata> {
        self.inner.backend().persistence_metadata()
    }
    pub fn has_conflict(&self) -> bool { self.conflict_pending }
    pub fn set_conflict(&mut self) { self.conflict_pending = true }
    pub fn clear_conflict(&mut self) { self.conflict_pending = false }
    pub fn set_conflict_pending(&mut self, v: bool) { self.conflict_pending = v }

    // ── Read pass-throughs and kanban-specific business logic ──────
    // boards/cards/columns/sprints/archived_cards/graph/snapshot/apply_snapshot
    // migrate_sprint_logs, archive_cards_detailed, move_cards_detailed, ...
    // All unchanged in body, only s/self.backend/self.inner.backend()/
    // and s/self.undo_stack.clear()/self.inner.clear_history()/
    // and s/self.dirty = true/self.inner.mark_dirty()/
}

// KanbanOperations and GraphOperations impl blocks — unchanged.
