  - We already know the pre-migration version at `:90` (`pre_migrate_version: Option<u32>`), and have `path_buf` (`:53`).
- `SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSION: u32 = 3` (`mod.rs:27`).
- No `VACUUM INTO` / file-copy anywhere in the crate; the only "backup" concept is the sidecar cleanup helper `cleanup_destination_files` in `kanban-service/src/store_manager.rs` (appends `-wal`/`-shm`), which is unrelated.
- JSON reference pattern (durable-on-*failure* only): `crates/kanban-persistence-json/src/migration/backup.rs::pre_latest_backup_path_for` returns `<path>.v{N}.backup`; the migrator writes it before the chain and removes it on success.

## Target
Add a helper that writes a **durable** pre-migration snapshot, invoked from `open()` immediately before the first schema-mutating step, only when an existing DB is below the supported version:

```rust
// crates/kanban-persistence-sqlite/src/sqlite_store/init.rs
impl SqliteStore {
    /// Durable, transactionally-consistent copy of the DB written to
    /// `<db_path>.schema<from_version>.backup` before an IRREVERSIBLE schema
    /// upgrade, so a user can roll back after downgrading the binary. Kept on
    /// success (unlike the migration's own transaction, which only guards a
    /// mid-migration crash). No-op if a backup already exists (a prior run's
    /// snapshot is still a valid pre-upgrade copy - never clobber it).
    ///
    /// Uses `VACUUM INTO`: a single consistent file (no `-wal`/`-shm`
    /// sidecars, no manual checkpoint). NOTE: `VACUUM INTO` takes a string
    /// LITERAL, not a bind parameter, so the path is interpolated with single
    /// quotes escaped.
    pub(crate) async fn write_pre_migration_backup(
        pool: &sqlx::Pool<sqlx::Sqlite>,
        db_path: &std::path::Path,
        from_version: u32,
    ) -> KanbanResult<()> { /* see Implementation example */ }
}
```

Call site in `open()` (between the future-version check ~`:98` and `migrate_v2_to_v3_archived_cards` ~`:111`):

```rust
if metadata_table_exists {
    if let Some(v) = pre_migrate_version {
        if v < SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSION {
            Self::write_pre_migration_backup(&pool, &path_buf, v).await?;
        }
    }
}
```

Design it **generic over `from_version`** (not hardcoded to 2) so the next schema bump inherits it for free.

