## Entity-specific quirks
- `VACUUM INTO` **cannot run inside a transaction** and takes a **literal** target path - escape `'` as `''`. The pool connection at `open()` time has no open tx, so this is fine.
- `VACUUM INTO` **fails if the target already exists** - the "no-op if present" guard also avoids that error path.
- The backup is a **full-size copy** of the DB (fine for typical board sizes; note it in the log line so users understand disk usage).
- Failure policy: **propagate the error (abort the open) by default** - do not perform an irreversible upgrade if we could not snapshot first. (Alternative: best-effort `log + proceed` if aborting on a read-only/full disk is deemed too strict - call this out for the reviewer to decide.)
- Path naming: **append**, do not use `with_extension` (which would drop `.sqlite`): `board.sqlite` -> `board.sqlite.schema2.backup`.

## Related consideration (note, not in scope)
For consistency, decide whether the JSON `V7->V8` format bump should ALSO leave a durable (kept-on-success) backup rather than only its transient crash-safety `.v7.backup`. If yes, that is a sibling change in `kanban-persistence-json`; file separately or fold into a shared "durable pre-format-bump backup" policy.

## Implementation example
```rust
// crates/kanban-persistence-sqlite/src/sqlite_store/init.rs
use std::path::Path;
use sqlx::{Pool, Sqlite};

impl SqliteStore {
    pub(crate) async fn write_pre_migration_backup(
        pool: &Pool<Sqlite>,
        db_path: &Path,
        from_version: u32,
    ) -> KanbanResult<()> {
        // Append (don't replace the extension) so the original name is preserved:
        // board.sqlite -> board.sqlite.schema2.backup
        let mut backup = db_path.as_os_str().to_owned();
        backup.push(format!(".schema{from_version}.backup"));
        let backup = std::path::PathBuf::from(backup);

        // Never clobber a prior snapshot - it is still a valid pre-upgrade copy.
        if backup.exists() {
            tracing::info!(
                path = %backup.display(),
                "pre-migration SQLite backup already present; keeping it"
            );
            return Ok(());
        }

        // VACUUM INTO wants a string LITERAL, not a bind param. Escape quotes.
        let target = backup.to_string_lossy().replace('\'', "''");
        sqlx::query(&format!("VACUUM INTO '{target}'"))
            .execute(pool)
            .await
            .map_err(db_err)?;

        tracing::warn!(
            path = %backup.display(),
            from_version,
            to_version = SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSION,
            "wrote durable pre-migration SQLite backup before irreversible schema upgrade"
        );
        Ok(())
    }
}
```

