## Target
### 1. `board.rs` — add the marker field + helpers
```rust
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize)]
pub struct Board {
    // ...existing fields, ending with created_at / updated_at...
    /// Archive marker. `None` = live (in the live board set); `Some(ts)` =
    /// archived at `ts` (the discrete archived-board collection). The board's
    /// subtree stays in place; archiving is a pure marker flip (D3/D4).
    #[serde(default)]
    pub archived_at: Option<DateTime<Utc>>,
}

impl Board {
    pub fn is_archived(&self) -> bool {
        self.archived_at.is_some()
    }

    /// Set the archive marker. Pure flip — touches ONLY `archived_at` so the
    /// archive/restore toggle is a lossless inverse (does NOT bump updated_at).
    pub fn archive(&mut self, at: DateTime<Utc>) {
        self.archived_at = Some(at);
    }

    /// Clear the archive marker (restore). Pure flip.
    pub fn unarchive(&mut self) {
        self.archived_at = None;
    }
}
```
