## Target
### 1. Two symmetric marker commands (`board_commands.rs`)
```rust
/// Archive a board: set its `archived_at` marker. The subtree stays in place
/// (D3). Reversible via RestoreBoard (D4/D5).
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct ArchiveBoard {
    pub board_id: Uuid,
}

/// Restore an archived board: clear its `archived_at` marker.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct RestoreBoard {
    pub board_id: Uuid,
}
```
Enum + three dispatch matches:
```rust
pub enum BoardCommand {
    // ...existing...
    ArchiveBoard(ArchiveBoard),
    RestoreBoard(RestoreBoard),
}
// execute / description / capture_inverse: add
//   BoardCommand::ArchiveBoard(c) => c.execute(context) / c.description() / c.capture_inverse(store),
//   BoardCommand::RestoreBoard(c) => ...
```
`ArchiveBoard` — marker set (a flip; no gather, no removal):
```rust
impl ArchiveBoard {
    pub fn execute(&self, context: &CommandContext) -> KanbanResult<()> {
        context.store.archive_board(self.board_id, Utc::now())
    }
    pub fn description(&self) -> String {
        format!("Archive board {}", self.board_id)
    }
    /// Symmetric inverse. capture_inverse runs BEFORE execute, but the inverse
    /// RestoreBoard executes during undo AFTER the forward archive, so the
    /// board is already archived when RestoreBoard runs — no payload needed.
    pub fn capture_inverse(&self, store: &dyn DataStore) -> KanbanResult<Vec<Command>> {
        if store.get_board(self.board_id)?.is_none() {
            return Err(KanbanError::not_found("Board", self.board_id));
        }
        Ok(vec![Command::Board(BoardCommand::RestoreBoard(RestoreBoard {
            board_id: self.board_id,
        }))])
    }
}
```
`RestoreBoard` — marker clear, mirror-symmetric:
```rust
impl RestoreBoard {
    pub fn execute(&self, context: &CommandContext) -> KanbanResult<()> {
        context.store.restore_board(self.board_id)
    }
    pub fn description(&self) -> String {
        format!("Restore board {}", self.board_id)
    }
    pub fn capture_inverse(&self, store: &dyn DataStore) -> KanbanResult<Vec<Command>> {
        if store.get_board(self.board_id)?.is_none() {
            return Err(KanbanError::not_found("Board", self.board_id));
        }
        Ok(vec![Command::Board(BoardCommand::ArchiveBoard(ArchiveBoard {
            board_id: self.board_id,
        }))])
    }
}
```
> Both inverses guard on `get_board` (not `list_archived_boards`) because `get_board(id)` is marker-agnostic — it returns the board whether live or archived (see store note below). That is exactly what makes the symmetric toggle work.

### 2. `DataStore` methods — functional defaults where possible (D6), `unsupported` only where not
```rust
// crates/kanban-domain/src/data_store.rs  (Board section, after delete_board :12)

/// Archived boards: the discrete `archived_at IS NOT NULL` collection.
/// NO functional default — `list_boards` is LIVE-ONLY (see below), so the
/// trait exposes no way to see archived boards generically. Each backend
/// overrides (in-memory here; SQLite in C5; the JSON backend forwards in C3).
fn list_archived_boards(&self) -> KanbanResult<Vec<Board>> {
    Err(KanbanError::unsupported("list_archived_boards"))
}

/// Set a board's archive marker. FUNCTIONAL DEFAULT via get + upsert — works
/// for every backend unchanged (a marker flip, no schema knowledge needed).
fn archive_board(&self, board_id: Uuid, at: chrono::DateTime<chrono::Utc>) -> KanbanResult<()> {
    let mut board = self
        .get_board(board_id)?
        .ok_or_else(|| KanbanError::not_found("Board", board_id))?;
    board.archive(at);
    self.upsert_board(board)
}

/// Clear a board's archive marker. FUNCTIONAL DEFAULT via get + upsert.
fn restore_board(&self, board_id: Uuid) -> KanbanResult<()> {
    let mut board = self
        .get_board(board_id)?
        .ok_or_else(|| KanbanError::not_found("Board", board_id))?;
    board.unarchive();
    self.upsert_board(board)
}
```
> Only `list_archived_boards` needs the `unsupported` affordance (F1a). `archive_board`/`restore_board` are pure `get_board`+`upsert_board` compositions, so their default is correct on ALL backends — no override required. This is the D6 "functional default keeps every slice green" principle applied maximally: two of the three new methods need no per-backend work.

### 3. **`list_boards` becomes LIVE-ONLY** (the one semantic change) — in-memory override
This is the single filter point that makes archived boards disappear from every live, board-scoped view (the boards panel, board-scoped card/column/sprint queries all navigate from `list_boards`). `get_board(id)` stays marker-agnostic so restore/permanent-delete can still find archived boards by id.
```rust
// in_memory_store/boards.rs
pub(super) fn list_boards_impl(&self) -> KanbanResult<Vec<Board>> {
    let state = self.read_state()?;
    let mut boards: Vec<Board> = state
        .boards
        .values()
        .filter(|b| !b.is_archived())   // LIVE ONLY (archived_at IS NULL)
        .cloned()
        .collect();
    boards.sort_by_key(|b| b.position);
    Ok(boards)
}

pub(super) fn list_archived_boards_impl(&self) -> KanbanResult<Vec<Board>> {
    let state = self.read_state()?;
    let mut boards: Vec<Board> = state
        .boards
        .values()
        .filter(|b| b.is_archived())    // archived_at IS NOT NULL
        .cloned()
        .collect();
    boards.sort_by(|a, b| b.archived_at.cmp(&a.archived_at)); // most-recent first
    Ok(boards)
}
// mod.rs: override `list_archived_boards` on DataStore for InMemoryStore -> list_archived_boards_impl
// (archive_board/restore_board inherit the functional default; no override needed.)
```
`state.boards` stays a SINGLE map — no `archived_boards` map (D3: the board stays in place, only the marker distinguishes it).

### 3b. Fix `ImportEntities::execute` dedup to be marker-agnostic (REQUIRED — the live-only `list_boards` fallout)
```rust
// board_commands.rs ImportEntities::execute (~:403) — BEFORE
let existing_board_ids: HashSet<Uuid> =
    context.store.list_boards()?.iter().map(|b| b.id).collect();
// AFTER — include archived boards so an import can't collide with an archived id
let existing_board_ids: HashSet<Uuid> = context
    .store
    .list_boards()?
    .iter()
    .chain(context.store.list_archived_boards()?.iter())
    .map(|b| b.id)
    .collect();
```
> **SPIKE-CORRECTED — "explicit unsupported is fine" was WRONG.** Making `list_boards` live-only AND having `ImportEntities` dedup call `list_archived_boards()` means **every backend whose `list_boards` is live-only MUST implement `list_archived_boards`** — otherwise it hits the `unsupported` default and **`create_board` BRICKS** (create routes through `ImportEntities` → dedup → `list_archived_boards()` → `unsupported` error/panic). The manual-impl backends (`JsonDataStore`, `SqliteBackend`'s hand-written `DataStore`) do NOT inherit `InMemoryStore`'s override, so they cannot be left on the default. Required fixes (coordinated with C3/C5): **`JsonDataStore` forwards `list_archived_boards` to its inner `InMemoryStore`; `SqliteBackend` filters `list_boards` by `is_archived()` as an interim** (empty until C5 persists the marker, then C5 swaps in the real `WHERE` query). This is an INVARIANT, not a "nice to have".

### 4. In-memory snapshot: partition boards by marker
```rust
// in_memory_store/snapshot.rs snapshot_impl — partition the ONE map by marker
let (archived_boards, live_boards): (Vec<Board>, Vec<Board>) =
    state.boards.values().cloned().partition(|b| b.is_archived());
// live_boards sorted by position (as today); archived_boards sorted by archived_at desc
let mut snap = Snapshot::from_data(live_boards, columns, cards, archived_cards, sprints, graph);
snap.archived_boards = archived_boards;   // C1 field; from_data stays 6-arg
Ok(snap)

// apply_snapshot_impl — merge BOTH partitions back into the one map
state.boards = snapshot
    .boards
    .into_iter()
    .chain(snapshot.archived_boards.into_iter())
    .map(|b| (b.id, b))
    .collect();
// ...rest unchanged (columns/cards/etc. carry the archived board's subtree in place)
```
> This is the correctness lynchpin: because `list_boards` is now live-only, `snapshot_impl` MUST pull archived boards from the raw map into `archived_boards`, or they vanish on save. The subtree (columns/cards/sprints/edges) is captured by the existing flat-collection reads unchanged — nothing extra to gather.

