## Entity-specific quirks
- **No animation for boards.** Unlike cards (which animate archive/restore/delete via `AnimationType` keyed by `card_id`), boards have no animated widget; all three operations are synchronous like column delete. Do not force card animations onto boards.
- **Two selection cursors.** `selection.board` (live) and the new `selection.archived_board` (archived view) are distinct; leaving the archived view must not disturb the live cursor, and each destructive/restore op clamps its own cursor.
- **`A` = archive (reversible, no confirm)** mirrors card `d` (no confirm — it is undoable). Only **permanent delete** (`x` in the archived view) is gated by a confirm popup, because it is the one irreversible-by-normal-undo-flow destructive action in this surface.
- **Key-scheme note.** Cards use lowercase = act / uppercase = view; A1 already put board delete on uppercase `D`, so this card uses uppercase `A` = archive (matching `D`'s "significant board op on the shifted key") and lowercase `a` = view archived. Document this in the help text so the asymmetry with the cards panel is intentional and visible.

