## Dependencies / sequencing
- **Depends on C3** (`archive_board`/`restore_board`/`list_archived_boards`/`delete_archived_board` on `KanbanOperations`; the `ArchivedBoard` domain type and `ArchivedBoardResponse` API DTO; optionally an archived-board resolver). Additive on top of C3 — compiles green once C3 lands.
- Independent of C6 (TUI) and C7 (CLI); surface cards land in any order after C3. MCP-only files: `tools/board.rs`, `requests/board.rs`, `requests/mod.rs`, `context.rs`, `helpers`.
- Not a DataStore-trait slice; the D6 default-`Unsupported` mitigation is carried by C3, not here.

## Entity-specific quirks
- **Namespace-correct resolution.** `archive` resolves against live boards (`mcp_resolve_board`); `restore` and `delete-archived` resolve against the archived set (`mcp_resolve_archived_board`). A live and an archived board may share a name (original IDs/names preserved per D4), so never cross the namespaces.
- **`restore` returns a full `BoardResponse`**; `archive`/`delete-archived` return terse id acks — matching the card tools (`restore_card` → `CardResponse`; `archive`/`delete` → `{"archived"/"deleted": id}`).
- **Auto-registration.** Because the new tools live in the existing `#[tool_router(router = board_router)]` block, they are exposed through the already-composed `Self::board_router()` in `lib.rs:64` — no edit to the router `+`-chain is required. Confirm the tools appear in a `list_tools` round-trip if such a test exists.

